**What I implemented:** `translate()` splits on whitespace and translates each word; `_translate_word()` appends `ay` for vowel/`xr`/`yt` starts (rule 1), otherwise finds the split point at the first vowel-or-medial-`y` from index 1 — extending past a `qu` pair (rules 3) — and reattaches the leading consonant/`qu` prefix with `ay`. **How verified:** executed 25 cases (all prompt examples + Exercism standard set) → 25/25 pass; `py_compile` and import clean; existing `script/linux/start.sh` smoke check OK; artifact assertion exit 0; independent reviewer verdict clean. No test files were created or modified (evidence logged outside `tests/` per the harness constraint).
